--[[
	HudArt -- ReplicatedStorage/Assets/Images

	Art for the always-on HUD (vitals bars, the XP bar). Sources live in assets/ui/hud/.
	An empty id means the code draws its own fallback, so art drops in piece by piece.

		BAR_GRAIN      256x32 seamless (left/right) dark swirls on transparent, laid over every
		               HudBarStyle fill and drifted slowly. Generated by script, not painted.
		GLOW_SOFT      128x128 white radial glow on transparent (bright core, soft falloff),
		               tinted per use: the XP bar's light orbs and their absorb flare.
		               Generated by script.
		XP_MEDALLION_FRAME  the combat XP bar's medallion: an oak-branch wreath drawn around a dark
		               disc that holds the combat icon (both drawn by the game). Empty: a plain
		               bronze ring instead.
		XP_MEDALLION_FRAME_ASPECT  its width / height.
		XP_MEDALLION_FRAME_HOLE    the empty middle: X/Y = its centre and D = its diameter, as
		               fractions of the image width (X, D) and height (Y). The disc goes there.
		ZONE_TREE      white tree silhouette, soft edges in its alpha, behind the REGION DISCOVERED
		               banner (ZoneClient), tinted gold there. Source: assets/ui/hud/zone_discovery_tree.png.
		ZONE_TREE_ASPECT  its width / height.

	Tried and dropped 2026-10-01: a leaf-and-brass end cap for the vitals bars (read badly at
	that size); the bars keep their iron diamonds.
]]

return {
	BAR_GRAIN = "rbxassetid://100183735763345", -- bar_grain.png
	GLOW_SOFT = "rbxassetid://119483079370092", -- glow_soft.png
	-- xp_medallion_frame.png (2026-10-01, "Cartoon Oak Leaf Wreath Frame"): a living oak branch
	-- bent into a ring, two-tone cel shading, acorn pair on the right. Hole measured from alpha.
	XP_MEDALLION_FRAME = "rbxassetid://90433944253668",
	XP_MEDALLION_FRAME_ASPECT = 1024 / 949,
	XP_MEDALLION_FRAME_HOLE = { X = 0.521, Y = 0.493, D = 0.532 },
	ZONE_TREE = "rbxassetid://111064666897495", -- zone_discovery_tree.png (2026-10-02)
	ZONE_TREE_ASPECT = 1023 / 667,
}
